# M-astronomia × M-chimica, attraverso l'unico nome che vive in due aree.
#
# `mercury` sta in due tavole curate, entrambe gia' residenti nella KB:
#
#   astronomia   planet_order(mercury, 1)   rocky_world(mercury)   orbits(mercury, sun)
#   chimica      atomic_number(mercury, 80) chemical_symbol(mercury, Hg)
#
# A scegliere l'area e' la domanda, non il nome. Il controllo negativo e'
# `earth`, che vive solo in astronomia: chiederne il simbolo chimico non deve
# produrre un simbolo. Nessuna conoscenza viene iniettata dal test.

[mock live]
!set PARROT0_SESSION=
!set PARROT0_LANG=en
!set PARROT0_TOOLS=1
!reset

[test the same name answers from the astronomy area]
!timeout 12
> is mercury a planet?
< Yes.

[test the same name answers from the chemistry area]
> what is the symbol of mercury?
< Hg.

[test the astronomy area keeps deciding on the same name]
> is mercury terrestrial?
< Yes.

[test astronomy does not concede the chemical conclusion]
> is mercury habitable?
< No.

[test a name that lives only in astronomy gets no chemical symbol]
> what is the symbol of earth?
< I don't know about symbol.
